     Build note: `fmpq_gcd(g->q, N->q, C->q)` with g, N, C all `adf_rat_t` (locals plus the
     const parameter) triggered a GCC -O2 -Wstringop-overread false positive ("reading 16
     bytes from a region of size 8"), turned into a hard error by -Werror; a minimal two-line
     repro without adf_fball did not reproduce it, so it is specific to this call shape.
     Worked around by copying through plain fmpq_t temporaries (fmpq_set, fmpq_set_fmpz_frac)
     before the fmpq_gcd call, never passing the struct-field expression `X->q` directly as a
     fmpq_gcd argument. No behaviour change; noted here in case another lane's code hits the
     same GCC quirk.

